# Consensus seal — SHA3-256 manifest. AUTO-GENERATED by `make core-seal`.
# Do not edit by hand. `make core-seal-check` fails loud if any sealed file drifts from this.
# Sealed set: core/ (consensus predicates + parameter tables) plus
# the block-connection ordering layer named in the Makefile's
# CORE_SEAL_PATHS (an ordering bug forks exactly as hard as a
# predicate bug — see docs/adr/0002-sealed-consensus-core.md).
#
# Format, in emitted order. Every line has exactly ONE parse: each
# variable-length field is either last on its line or length-prefixed,
# and a sealable path may not contain a control byte.
#
#   <sha3-256 hex>  <path>
#       One per sealed file, path-sorted. 64 lowercase hex, two spaces,
#       then the path as the rest of the line.
#
#   SECTION  <files>  <pathlen>  <hex>  <path>
#       One per directory holding sealed files, path-sorted. <files> is
#       RECURSIVE; <pathlen> is the exact byte length of <path>, which is
#       the rest of the line (so a path containing spaces round-trips).
#       <hex> is that directory's node digest in cognition/modules/codeindex's source
#       Merkle dialect (codeindex_merkle.c):
#         leaf = SHA3-256(0x10 || "zcl.codeindex.merkle.leaf.v1\0"
#                         || relpath\0 || u64le(size) || bytes)
#         node = SHA3-256(0x11 || "zcl.codeindex.merkle.node.v1\0"
#                         || dirpath\0 || u32le(nkids)
#                         || for each child: kind || name\0 || digest)
#       Children are ordered by strcmp over the child's name, plus '/'
#       for a directory. N-ary, so there is no leaf-pairing and no
#       duplicate-tail ambiguity; tag 0x10 vs 0x11 plus the domain
#       strings separate leaves from interior nodes.
#
#   TREE  <hex>
#       The root node (dirpath "") over the whole sealed set, same dialect.
#
#   ROOT  <hex>
#       FINAL LINE. The flat fold over every sorted `path \0 filehash`
#       pair — the sealed core's identity, mirrored into
#       hotswap/core_seal_root.h. FROZEN: SECTION/TREE are additive and
#       do not enter this preimage.
